# Changelog

## [0.3.1.14]

### Added
- `fits_to_ms` adds discovered AIPS UVFLG station artifacts to existing IDI/MS
  flagging, with `apply_flag_from_artifacts`, `artifact_flag_extensions`, and
  `artifact_flagfiles` options. Conversion reuses JIVE keyin parsing, normalizes
  day-of-year times, and honors TIMEOFF, DTIMRANG, reasons and IF/channel ranges.
- Artifact commands are deduplicated per output MS; invalid/irrelevant records
  are reported in a JSON sidecar. Unique before/after flag versions preserve
  rerun backups. Existing MSs retain the apply_flag_to_existing_vis opt-in.
- `artifact_dirs`, `use_local_antab`, and `local_antab_require_full_array` options to `pipe config`.
- existing antab is used when available in `artifact_dirs`, `folder_for_fits` or `<workdir>/raw`.
- local antab selection requires more than `valid_perc` overlap with the UV data
  for matching antennas. Partial station calibration is accepted by default,
  with warnings for missing antennas; full-array coverage is an opt-in check.
  IF mismatch remains a warning.
- eligible candidates are ranked by time coverage, antenna coverage, and IF
  agreement; equal ranks raise an ambiguity error. Malformed and unrelated
  candidates are skipped before falling back to VLBA calibration retrieval.
- candidate decisions and calibration sources are recorded in preprocessing metadata.

### Fixed
- VLBA archive fallback reads HTML row strings consistently and constructs the
  nested project/jobs URLs correctly, avoiding the obsolete `get_text()` call.
- `TIMEOFF=*` in an ANTAB is read as `TIMEOFF=0`, with a printed and logged warning,
  instead of failing the keyin parser.
- an empty `POLY=` is now refused with an explicit error rather than being written or
  silently treated as unity gain; discovery skips such candidates.
- appending calibration preserves existing gains for uncovered antennas and TSYS
  outside the incoming per-antenna/array/frequency time spans. Empty imported tables
  and incompatible merge schemas fail before staged files replace working data.

## [0.3.1.13]

### Fixed
- `--default` for `pipe config` now preserves the existing config.
- `snr_threshold_phref` was misspelled, corrected.

